# Line endings, pinned per file type.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf checks files out
# with CRLF. That is fine for Python and Markdown, and fatal for a shell
# script: Linux reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` as a request for an interpreter
# literally named "bash\r" and fails with a confusing "bad interpreter" or
# "no such file or directory". An install script that only works on the
# machine it was written on is not much of an install script.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the opposite case: keep it CRLF so it behaves in every Windows
# editor and console host.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never let a text filter touch binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.safetensors binary
